(4500025, 645699, 30807, '<td valign="top">Very nice idea! Creative and good use of shallow DOF. I''m guessing you superglued the rodent into a prepared hole in the loaf, OR you get 100% for patience! Either way, keep doing that thing you did to get this one - well done! Most deserved. I actually like the idea more than the first placed, which although a lovely shot, seems to be less thought-demanding than yours, though I bet the photographer had to wait and be very patient, or use remote and read a short novel while waiting.(I don''t really think you superglued it ("no animal was harmed whilst filming", etc...)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-20 06:06:21.</i></td>', 'Very nice idea! Creative and good use of shallow DOF. I''m guessing you superglued the rodent into a prepared hole in the loaf, OR you get 100% for patience! Either way, keep doing that thing you did to get this one - well done! Most deserved. I actually like the idea more than the first placed, which although a lovely shot, seems to be less thought-demanding than yours, though I bet the photographer had to wait and be very patient, or use remote and read a short novel while waiting.(I don''t really think you superglued it ("no animal was harmed whilst filming", etc...)', '2008-02-20 06:04:13.000000', '2008-02-20 06:06:21.000000', 0),
