(4782579, 646328, 24486, '<td valign="top">I really like your concept. At first glance, I wondered how many pieces of bread got toasted for this shot or how many times the same two pieces got ''popped''.The effort was well worth the result. I am going to make the assumption that your toaster is actually white &amp; that the colour produced in the photograph is a colour cast problem. Please forgive me if I''m wrong. To fix the colour cast problem is easy. You can either do it ''in camera'' by playing around in the white balance settings on your camera or if our editing software allows you to select the ''set white point'' then just bring that icon over any part of the toaster &amp; click &amp; that''s it, instant white toaster again.</td>', 'I really like your concept. At first glance, I wondered how many pieces of bread got toasted for this shot or how many times the same two pieces got ''popped''.The effort was well worth the result. I am going to make the assumption that your toaster is actually white & that the colour produced in the photograph is a colour cast problem. Please forgive me if I''m wrong. To fix the colour cast problem is easy. You can either do it ''in camera'' by playing around in the white balance settings on your camera or if our editing software allows you to select the ''set white point'' then just bring that icon over any part of the toaster & click & that''s it, instant white toaster again.', '2008-06-24 00:43:57.000000', NULL, 0),
